        "original_id": "dcae1fab-c00f-593b-8adb-9df93de3804a",
        "text": "Page: Lower Lake Stone Jail. Sentence: During the days of the first quicksilver operations of the Sulphur Bank Mine, lasting from 1873 to 1883, rapid town growth and the urgent need for civil order necessitated the building of a jail.\nPage: Sulphur Bank Mine. Sentence: The 150 acre mine became one of the most noted mercury producers in the world.\nPage: Eastlake, Lake County, California. Sentence: It was located just southwest of the Sulphur Bank Mine 7 mi north-northwest of Lower Lake, at an elevation of 1355 feet (413 m).",
